### The Preamble VDAF
- Mark presented [The Preamble VDAF](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ppm-the-preamble-vdaf-00), a new VDAF design targeted at large sparse histograms (e.g., high-dimensional categorization vectors like image classification).
- **Technical Mechanism**:
  - Addresses the linear communication overhead of Prio3 for high-dimensional vectors by leveraging Distributed Point Functions (DPF) / Function Secret Sharing (FSS).
  - Divides vectors into blocks and assumes block sparsity (non-zero entries concentrated in a single block) combined with fully linear proofs (FLP) evaluated per block.
- **Feedback & Discussion**:
  - Martin Thomson, Junyu, and Chris Patton noted that supporting multiple non-zero blocks would be a highly desirable enhancement for practical use cases.
  - The venue for standardization was discussed. Several participants (Tim Geoghegan, Martin Thomson, Chris Patton) noted that CFRG is generally slow for protocol-level specifications and code point management, though Tim Geoghegan highlighted that gaining production deployment experience should precede formal IETF standardization.
  - Deb Cooley emphasized that formal standards are necessary when cross-vendor interoperability is required.

### VDAF IANA Registry & Code Point Management
- The group discussed where the VDAF code point registry should be created and managed (in the CFRG VDAF specification vs. the IETF DAP specification [draft-ietf-ppm-dap](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-ppm-dap/)).
- Chris Patton noted that the CFRG VDAF draft currently requests IANA to create a "Specification Required" registry for VDAFs.
- Sam Weiler and Deb Cooley clarified that regardless of whether the registry is established via an IRTF or IETF document, it forms a standard IANA registry and does not require moving text between documents unless IANA raises an issue.

### MOL (MOLE) Integration
- Chris Patton summarized the MOL BOF held earlier in the week and its relationship to DAP.
- MOL requires reporting in aggregate which token issuer generated client credentials. Integrating this with DAP would primarily require a DAP report extension.
- Chris Wood noted that the DAP report extension registry in [draft-ietf-ppm-dap](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-ppm-dap/) is Specification Required, allowing MOL to define its necessary extensions in its own draft without reopening DAP.

